Z||000000||fiero56||10-11-2000||12:02 PM||||Today I called about an '86 Fiero I had seen on traderonline the other day. Called the guy up, checked it out, and I got myself a silver '86 SE(production #9,000 something) v-6 4-speed with 101,000 miles. It will be dropped off tomorrow afternoon. It needs some work, nothing major, but a few things need fixing, i.e. door locks are stiff, paint is bad, etc. I can't wait! I can hardly contain myself.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pffsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||william_thorniii||10-11-2000||12:32 PM||||56,<P>Congrats!  I still think that you should have bought my GT :~p  but I know that you will be happy with any Fiero you bought.  Hopefully we can get my 86 SE running tonight.  We could park it at your place and then your Fiero population could triple tomorrow.  I look forward to checking it out.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000002||fiero56||10-11-2000||12:38 PM||||Well, as of right now, my '86SE doesn't run either. The car belonged to the son of the guy who I talked with. They bought it 4 years ago, his son drove it for 3 years, until he had a second kid and needed a mini-van. It was parked in his fathers shop for about a year. He put the car up for sale the other week, and it wouldn't start when someone came to look at it. We checked it out, and there is no spark, ??? He did knock $100 off sine it wouldn't run. I got it for $500 flat. New tires, new brakes, new headliner, factory sub, interior is in excellent shape, needs paint, a little body work, and a few odds and ends, but I feel I got a deal.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||10-11-2000||12:56 PM||||Congratulations 56, welcome to the group of MFO (multiple Fiero Owners) -- If you need parts, don't forget where I am now - at the Fiero Shop -- you can call me at 1-510-23-FIERO (1-510-233-4376) any time...... Enjoy your SE!!<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                        <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||10-11-2000||10:22 PM||||I won't forget about you Terry. Seems like I was going to call you about something else, but don't remember what. There are a few small things I will need, but might be able to pick them up locally, at a j-yard. If not, I will give you a call.<P>The guy is also throwing in all his Fiero parts, a dash, and a box of "stuff."<P>First thing is get the engine running, but I am confident I can find the problem. Pictures of my dirty new baby, will be up Friday probably. I can't wait to row through the gears with a slick shifting 4-speed, instead of my notchy, grindy, stiff, jerky, Getrag. I can't believe GM introduced the Getrag as an improvement over the Muncie. What were they smoking.||||reg||1
