Z||000013||tgowens||10-12-2000||11:14 PM||||this is true -- we (Carolyn and I) just got our third one -- now there is a gold '87 GT, a blue '87 GT and her new medium red metallic  '87 GT (hmmmmmm, we seem to be stuck on '87s, huh??) -- now, when will I find the time to work on all of these cars?? (guess I'd better do her red one first, right?) -- The only way to get her posting here on the forum is to put her in a Fiero!!! (right, Honey??)<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                        <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000014||fiero56||10-13-2000||12:02 PM||||I am in class right now, but had a couple hours early this morning to play with the SE.<P>I gave it a general tun-up, along with a few known good spare parts I had laying around. It now idles perfectly, and solidly. I don't have the shift linkages adjusted yet, so haven't driven it. It does have a moderate stall for about a second at idle when I punch the throttle, but it does respond properly to throttle inputs after that. I found a bad "T" connection that connects the MAP to the plenum, replaced it and the MAP, but still have the stall. I am also questioning the heater core, but I am progressing.<P>Edited because I figure I will add this:<P>Pictures will be up later tonight. I will snap a few, and upload them here.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 10-13-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000015||william_thorniii||10-13-2000||04:36 PM||||This car is beautiful!  I had the pleasure of helping out Mr. Raymond last night.  Very impressive find for $500!<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000016||fiero56||10-14-2000||01:08 AM||||I won't buy much of anything big, unless it is a deal. The SE and Formula purchase prices combined have cost me $1,600. I didn't get around to getting pictures of the SE today, too busy trying to get the hesitation gone, and cleaning it up. Steam cleaned the carpet and seat on the driver side. Looks 200 times better. Passenger will be Saturday. Interior is coming along nicely. The exhaust note is awsome, much better(louder actually)than my Formula.||||reg||1
Z||000017||fiero56||10-16-2000||01:29 AM||||PICTURES!!! I finally got my computer to aknowledge my camera.<P>In the pics, I have the interior torn out for steam cleaning/fabreezr, so it isn't all there right now, but the parts/seat are in the garage. Pics are smaller for faster downloading, and less server space.<P><BR>Here they are:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1_12.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2_9.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/3_5.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4_4.jpg"> <P>How's this for a PFF calendar photo? If it isn't good enough, I can clean it up much better, and take better pictures.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/5_2.jpg"> ||||reg||6
